# Preserve shipping versions

Shipping releases are immutable. Versions exist so a known-good ship stays recoverable.

## N / N-1 rolling window

Keep the **last two** recoverable ships (**N** and **N-1**). See [docs/RESTORE.md](docs/RESTORE.md).

Current slots (do not delete tags or `out/` ISO dirs when cutting the next ship):

- **N:** `v0.8.8` / Drive + `out/v0.8.8/` / `checksums/v0.8.8.sha256` (`c5aa2305…`)
- **N-1:** `v0.8.7` / Drive + `out/v0.8.7/` / `checksums/v0.8.7.sha256` (`5e554919…`)

Older public/local ships (`v0.8.6`, `v0.8.5`, `v0.8.4`, …) are **outside** the rolling window. Tags/checksums may remain; local `out/` / Drive ISOs for those may be removed after N advances again.

**Retired:** early **v0.2.0** is outside the rolling window (checksum removed; not a restore slot). Prefer **v0.8.8** (or **v0.8.7** as restore).

**Do not flash `v0.3.5`** (truncated ISO).

## Never overwrite

- Do **not** move, retag, delete, or force-rewrite tag `v0.8.7`, `v0.8.8`, or any published shipping tag once cut.
- Do **not** change or replace published checksum files once shipped.
- Do **not** overwrite the Drive **v0.8.7** ISO under the same name if contents differ.
- Do **not** overwrite the Drive **v0.8.8** ISO under the same name if contents differ.
- Do **not** flash or publish a later build under an existing release name if contents differ.
- When cutting the next ship after **v0.8.8**, keep N/N-1 tags and their `out/<version>/` ISO directories; drop older slots from the rolling window as needed.

## New work gets new names

- New product work → new tag (`v0.8.9`, `v0.9.0`, …), new `out/<version>/StickLLM-vX.Y.Z.iso`, new checksum file.
- **Naming:** v0.3.7+ use exactly `StickLLM-vX.Y.Z.iso` (example: `StickLLM-v0.8.8.iso`). Through v0.3.6, published files stay `stickllm-amd-rtx3090-v….hybrid.iso` — never rename or rewrite those.
- Rebuilds of an older line → distinct `out/` path; never overwrite a shipping ISO name. Compare hash to the shipping checksum; report bit-identical if equal.
- WIP / abandoned experiments → branch only (`wip/…`); never replace a shipping tag or Drive ISO.

## Examples

```text
❌ BAD: build v0.8.3 and delete out/v0.8.2/ or tag -d v0.8.2
❌ BAD: build v0.8.2 and write over StickLLM-v0.8.1.iso on Drive
❌ BAD: git tag -f v0.8.8 <new-commit>
❌ BAD: edit checksums/v0.8.8.sha256 to match a different ISO

✅ GOOD: out/v0.8.5/StickLLM-v0.8.5.iso + checksums/v0.8.5.sha256 (N-1; leave as-is)
✅ GOOD: out/v0.8.6/StickLLM-v0.8.6.iso + checksums/v0.8.6.sha256 + tag v0.8.6
✅ GOOD: out/v0.8.7/StickLLM-v0.8.7.iso + checksums/v0.8.7.sha256 + tag v0.8.7 (keep prior N/N-1)
✅ GOOD: remove local out/v0.8.3/ or Drive StickLLM-v0.8.3.iso (outside rolling window)
```
